From 5f3d1df11b499c105e97b31837b4e1b08fddca1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pankaj Deopa <47059657+3-pi-radians@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:37:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add Native SSO requests to the Postman collection

New 'Native SSO' folder (22 requests): registers a Super App
(device_sso, device_sso_allowed_clients) and a Child App (token-exchange
grant), runs the Super App PAR + PKCE + DPoP (ES256) + OTP login reusing
the FAPI2.0 flow steps, checks device_secret, sid and ds_hash, performs
the Child App token exchange and userinfo with the Super App's DPoP key,
and covers repeat sign-in, narrower scope, device_sso on exchange,
scope beyond the grant (interaction_required), unrelated DPoP key,
missing DPoP proof, tampered/invalid and expired device secrets.
Scripts return a promise instead of using top-level await.
